{
  "slug": "llmprobe",
  "name": "Llmprobe",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Synthetic monitoring for LLM inference endpoints. Probe TTFT, latency, throughput, and errors across OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, Bedrock,   and any OpenAI-compatible server.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `llmprobe` (Check LLM API endpoint health, measure TTFT, latency, and throughput) and **1 MCP server**, `llmprobe`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install llmprobe@claude-community` from `Jwrede/llmprobe`.\n\nllmprobe is a CLI tool for LLM serving reliability. It probes hosted APIs or OpenAI-compatible inference servers, then reports the metrics that matter for production user experience: time to first token (TTFT), total latency, generation throughput (tokens/sec), and error rates.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "mcp": 1
  },
